{
  "requirement": "```rust,ignore\n// Method on Validator<D>.\n/// Encode the answer and atomically replace this source/criterion's record.\npub fn store_evidence<O: serde::Serialize>(\n    &self,\n    inputs: &Fingerprinted<D, O>,\n) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n```\n\nThe method saves under the source identity and criterion path captured in\n`Fingerprinted`, preserving its revision, input trace, and completed answer. Encoding follows\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.output`; atomic replacement follows\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage`. The result type needs\nno `Sync` bound: the method encodes the answer and captures the record and\nstorage key before constructing the storage future.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation of `requirements.sdk.graph.validation.store_evidence`. I found no gap.\n\n- **Save under the captured source identity and criterion path.** `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` stores records for the `behavior`, `structure` and `text` criteria of one source and loads each back. It asserts that the stored records are separate per criterion. `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets` and the `serialization_failure…` test also load by `(Node(1), path)` directly from storage.\n- **Preserve revision, input trace and completed answer.**\n  - `criteria_keep_typed_answers…` compares the loaded value's output, source id, criterion path, revision and dependencies with the stored value. It also checks the raw stored output JSON.\n  - `input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations` checks that the stored dependencies are the `Dependency::Node` entry with the new fingerprint.\n  - `agent_edge_tools…` checks that the stored `OutgoingEdges` dependency matches the one on the `Fingerprinted` value.\n  - `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error…` checks the stored `Dependency::Node(1, fp(\"root\"))`.\n- **Serialization failure returns `ValidationError::Output` and leaves the existing record unchanged.** `serialization_failure_leaves_the_existing_record_unchanged` stores an old record, then stores a value whose answer is `Unencodable`. It asserts `ValidationError::Output` with the message \"cannot encode answer\". It then asserts that the revision, dependencies and output are unchanged and that `writes == 1`, so no storage write happened.\n- **Storage failure returns `ValidationError::Graph`.** `resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments` sets `fail_store` and asserts `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"store\"))` and that no record was written.\n- **Atomic replacement, with one complete record after competing saves.** `concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records` runs two saves with different revisions, dependencies and outputs concurrently. It asserts that exactly one record remains and that its revision, dependencies and output all belong to the same save. It accepts either save winning, which matches the \"no ordering guaranteed\" wording. The replace-rather-than-append behavior is also checked in `typed_loading_reports_decode_errors_even_for_stale_evidence`, which asserts `records.len() == 1` after a second save.\n- **No `Sync` bound on the result type.** `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync` stores a `Cell<u32>` answer, which is `Send` but not `Sync`. It wraps the `store_evidence` future in `send`, which requires `T: Send`. That asserts the future is `Send` and compiles with a non-`Sync` answer. It then round-trips the value.\n- **Cited requirements.** `record.output` and `evidence_storage` are cited context. The Output/Graph error mapping and the unchanged record on failure are covered above. `malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_bad_outputs_are_output_errors` also exercises the real file-backed storage path.\n\nThe tests have `{test}` markers on the subject, and their assertions enforce the expected outcomes.",
  "references": "8e33ac85a20b563a55d309676c6dc74e14308b10a5a4cc7b94b85799c6b9f515",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.graph.validation.store_evidence",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.sdk.graph.validation.store_evidence"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} store_evidence",
        "```rust,ignore",
        "// Method on Validator<D>.",
        "/// Encode the answer and atomically replace this source/criterion's record.",
        "pub fn store_evidence<O: serde::Serialize>(",
        "    &self,",
        "    inputs: &Fingerprinted<D, O>,",
        ") -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;",
        "```",
        "",
        "The method saves under the source identity and criterion path captured in",
        "`Fingerprinted`, preserving its revision, input trace, and completed answer. Encoding follows",
        "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.output`; atomic replacement follows",
        "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage`. The result type needs",
        "no `Sync` bound: the method encodes the answer and captures the record and",
        "storage key before constructing the storage future.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.output",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.output"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} record.output",
        "`Validator::store_evidence` serializes the answer in `Fingerprinted` before passing",
        "the complete record to storage. A serialization failure returns",
        "`ValidationError::Output` and leaves the existing record unchanged. A storage",
        "failure returns `ValidationError::Graph`.",
        "",
        "`Validator::load_evidence` decodes a loaded record's output into the requested",
        "`Criterion::Ok`. An output that cannot decode returns `ValidationError::Output`,",
        "including when the saved revision or inputs are stale. Missing evidence returns",
        "`Ok(None)`; malformed stored records and storage failures return",
        "`ValidationError::Graph`. Revision and input comparison belong to the caller's",
        "reuse workflow under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.validation.procedure_identity`.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} evidence_storage",
        "```rust,ignore",
        "use std::future::Future;",
        "",
        "// Defined in habeas_sdk::graph.",
        "pub trait EvidenceStorage: Graph {",
        "    /// Ok(None) means absent; Err means loading failed.",
        "    fn load_evidence(",
        "        &self,",
        "        source: &Self::NodeId,",
        "        criterion: &CriterionPath,",
        "    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<",
        "        Option<Record<Self::NodeId, Self::EdgeLabel>>,",
        "        Self::Error,",
        "    >> + Send;",
        "",
        "    /// Atomically replace only this source/criterion pair's complete record.",
        "    fn store_evidence(",
        "        &self,",
        "        source: &Self::NodeId,",
        "        criterion: &CriterionPath,",
        "        record: &Record<Self::NodeId, Self::EdgeLabel>,",
        "    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), Self::Error>> + Send;",
        "}",
        "```",
        "",
        "The validator passes the source identity and criterion path to both methods. The",
        "key preserves both parts: source paths `[\"a\"]` and `[\"a\", \"b\"]` with criteria",
        "`[\"b\", \"c\"]` and `[\"c\"]` identify different records, even though flattening each",
        "pair would produce the same segments.",
        "",
        "Different criteria of a source have independent records. A revision change",
        "invalidates the same criterion's record rather than creating another key.",
        "The interface requires neither filesystem paths nor global evidence listing.",
        "",
        "Successful loads observe either an old or new complete record, or absence",
        "before the first save. Successful competing saves leave one complete record;",
        "its revision, dependencies, and output all belong to that save. No ordering",
        "between competing saves is guaranteed.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
